<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insultātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a springing</i> or
				<i>leaping over</i> or <i>on</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 52, 20</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>insolent
			behavior</i> towards any one, <i>a scoffing</i>, <i>reviling</i>, <i>insulting</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 8,
				5, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil insultatione barbarorum intolerantius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor. 4, 12, 36</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
